    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/rules/1-5-7-elementalist-benefits",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Elementalist Benefits",
      "slug": "1-5-7-elementalist-benefits",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.5.7",
        "heading": "Elementalist Benefits",
        "lineStart": 1071,
        "lineEnd": 1080
      },
      "section": "1.5.7",
      "rulesText": "All Elementalists gain Magic as a bonus skill, acquiring it at level-0, or level-1 if was already level-0.\n\nElementalists can prepare and cast High Magic spells in addition to the spells specific to Elementalists. As usual for spellcasters, Elementalists can’t cast spells or use arts while armored or holding a shield.\n\nElementalists are not as talented at general High Magic research as High Mages are, but their studies still bear fruit in time. Each time they advance a level, they can pick a new High Magic spell or an Elementalist spell to add to their spellbook. They must be able to cast the spell to add it to their selection.\n\nElementalists gain the Elemental Resilience and Elemental Sparks arts as part of their basic training, and may pick one additional art from the list below. Further arts are learned as they advance in character level, as given in the tables below. Once chosen, an art cannot be changed."
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/rules/1-5-7-the-elementalist",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "1.5.7 The Elementalist",
      "slug": "1-5-7-the-elementalist",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.5.7",
        "heading": "1.5.7 The Elementalist",
        "lineStart": 1067,
        "lineEnd": 1070
      },
      "section": "1.5.7",
      "rulesText": "Elementalists are spellcasting Mages who focus on the manipulation of the material world around them. While they are capable of using High Magic, their specialist spells focus chiefly on wielding the classical elements of fire, air, water, and earth."
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/rules/1-5-8-class-ability-masterful-expertise",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Class Ability: Masterful Expertise",
      "slug": "1-5-8-class-ability-masterful-expertise",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.5.8",
        "heading": "Class Ability: Masterful Expertise",
        "lineStart": 1209,
        "lineEnd": 1216
      },
      "section": "1.5.8",
      "rulesText": "Once per scene, a Full Expert may reroll any non-combat skill check as an Instant action. This allows the Expert to make a roll and then immediately use this ability if the resulting total isn’t good enough to succeed. In cases where it matters, the better of the two rolls may be used.\n\nNote that the typical ten-minute dungeon exploration turn generally counts as a scene, allowing the Full Expert to use this ability every turn if they so wish.\n\nPartial Experts do not receive this ability."
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/rules/1-5-8-class-ability-quick-learner",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Class Ability: Quick Learner",
      "slug": "1-5-8-class-ability-quick-learner",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.5.8",
        "heading": "Class Ability: Quick Learner",
        "lineStart": 1217,
        "lineEnd": 1222
      },
      "section": "1.5.8",
      "rulesText": "When you advance a character level, you gain an extra skill point which may only be spent on gaining or improving non-combat skills or raising attributes. You may save this point to spend later if you wish.\n\nPartial Experts do receive this ability."
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/rules/1-5-8-full-expert",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Full Expert",
      "slug": "1-5-8-full-expert",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.5.8",
        "heading": "Full Expert",
        "lineStart": 1223,
        "lineEnd": 1237
      },
      "section": "1.5.8",
      "rulesText": "|Level|Hit Dice|Attack<br>Bonus|Focus Picks|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|1|1d6|+0|1 Expert<br>+1 Any|\n|2|2d6|+1|+1 Any|\n|3|3d6|+1||\n|4|4d6|+2||\n|5|5d6|+2|+1 Any|\n|6|6d6|+3||\n|7|7d6|+3|+1 Any|\n|8|8d6|+4||\n|9|9d6|+4||\n|10|10d6|+5|+1 Any|"
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/rules/1-5-8-partial-mage-partial-expert",
