          "result": "Shooting a bow or crossbow while in melee",
          "cells": [
            "Shooting a bow or crossbow while in melee",
            "N/A"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 10,
          "result": "You are shooting at a target you can’t see but you know where they are.",
          "cells": [
            "You are shooting at a target you can’t see but you know where they are.",
            "-4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 11,
          "result": "You are shooting at a target you can’t see and don’t know their exact position.",
          "cells": [
            "You are shooting at a target you can’t see and don’t know their exact position.",
            "N/A"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "rulesText": "Some common situations can modify an attack roll, granting a bonus or penalty. GMs may add others depending on the situation.\n\n|Situation|Mod|\n|---|---|\n|Shooting at a distant prone foe|-2|\n|Attacking an adjacent prone foe|+2|\n|Melee attacking while prone|-4|\n|Your target is past your bow or thrown weapon’s normal<br>range, up to its maximum long range.|-2|\n|The target is at least half behind cover|-2|\n|The target is almost completely in cover|-4|\n|Making a thrown attack while in melee|-4|\n|Throwing a weapon while in melee|-4|\n|Shooting a bow or crossbow while in melee|N/A|\n|You are shooting at a target you can’t see but you know<br>where they are.|-4|\n|You are shooting at a target you can’t see and don’t<br>know their exact position.|N/A|"
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/tables/2-6-1-foot-chases",
      "@type": "Table",
      "name": "2.6.1 Foot Chases",
      "slug": "2-6-1-foot-chases",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "2.6.1",
        "heading": "2.6.1 Foot Chases",
        "lineStart": 3037,
        "lineEnd": 3055
      },
      "tableType": "2.6.1 Foot Chases",
      "columns": [
        "Situation",
        "Mod"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "position": 1,
          "result": "There are more pursuers than pursued",
          "cells": [
            "There are more pursuers than pursued",
            "-1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 2,
          "result": "The pursued have no head start at all",
          "cells": [
            "The pursued have no head start at all",
            "+2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 3,
          "result": "The pursued have one round’s head start",
          "cells": [
            "The pursued have one round’s head start",
            "+1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 4,
          "result": "The pursued have less than a minute’s head start",
          "cells": [
            "The pursued have less than a minute’s head start",
            "+0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 5,
          "result": "The pursued have more than a minute’s head start",
          "cells": [
            "The pursued have more than a minute’s head start",
            "-2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 6,
          "result": "Who knows the local terrain better?",
          "cells": [
            "Who knows the local terrain better?",
            "-2 to +2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 7,
          "result": "The pursuit is half-hearted or obligatory",
          "cells": [
            "The pursuit is half-hearted or obligatory",
            "-1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 8,
          "result": "The pursuers are enraged or vengeful",
          "cells": [
            "The pursuers are enraged or vengeful",
            "+1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "rulesText": "The group member in the fleeing party with the best Dex/Exert or Con/Exert total rolls a skill check. Their result is the fleeing group’s pace, as they help and encourage the slower members.\n\nOther fleeing group members then hinder pursuit in whatever ways they think are helpful. Sometimes a skill check is needed, while other times a GM will simply decide it works. Each successful effort adds a +1 bonus to the pace, up to +3 maximum. Botched efforts are either unhelpful or apply a -1 penalty if they’re actively harmful. If the fleeing group is made up of NPCs, it’s the GM’s judgment as to whether any of them try to do something clever to stall the PCs.\n\nThe pursuing group then makes a single Dex/Exert or Con/Exert skill check, modified by the table below. If they beat the fleeing group’s total they catch up to them, and if they tie or roll less the fleeing party has escaped immediate pursuit.\n\n|Situation|Mod|\n|---|---|\n|There are more pursuers than pursued|-1|\n|The pursued have no head start at all|+2|\n|The pursued have one round’s head start|+1|\n|The pursued have less than a minute’s head start|+0|\n|The pursued have more than a minute’s head start|-2|\n|Who knows the local terrain better?|-2 to +2|\n|The pursuit is half-hearted or obligatory|-1|\n|The pursuers are enraged or vengeful|+1|"
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/tables/2-6-2-mounted-chases",
      "@type": "Table",
      "name": "2.6.2 Mounted Chases",
      "slug": "2-6-2-mounted-chases",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "2.6.2",
        "heading": "2.6.2 Mounted Chases",
        "lineStart": 3056,
        "lineEnd": 3073
      },
      "tableType": "2.6.2 Mounted Chases",
      "columns": [
        "Situation",
        "Modifier"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "position": 1,
          "result": "The pursuer can’t directly see the pursued",
          "cells": [
            "The pursuer can’t directly see the pursued",
            "-2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 2,
          "result": "The pursuer is flying but the pursued isn’t",
          "cells": [
            "The pursuer is flying but the pursued isn’t",
            "+3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 3,
          "result": "The pursued is flying but the pursuer isn’t",
          "cells": [
            "The pursued is flying but the pursuer isn’t",
            "-3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 4,
          "result": "A spotter is relaying the target’s position",
          "cells": [
            "A spotter is relaying the target’s position",
            "+1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 5,
          "result": "Who knows the local terrain better?",
          "cells": [
            "Who knows the local terrain better?",
            "-2 to +2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 6,
          "result": "The pursuit is half-hearted or obligatory",
          "cells": [
            "The pursuit is half-hearted or obligatory",
            "-1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 7,
          "result": "The pursuers are enraged or vengeful",
          "cells": [
            "The pursuers are enraged or vengeful",
            "+1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "rulesText": "For mounted or vehicular chases, the fleeing rider makes a Ride skill check, usually modified by Dexterity. This is the fleeing mount’s pace.\n\nEach pursuer then makes its own Dex/Ride skill check to catch up with the quarry, modified by the table below. Any of them who don’t equal or exceed the fleeing mount’s pace fall behind and are lost from the pursuit. Any of them who do make the roll catch up to the mount, and it usually becomes a matter of combat until the quarry can make another escape attempt or win the ensuing battle.\n\nUnmounted pursuers cannot generally hope to catch up with mounted evaders over a short-term chase.\n\n|Situation|Modifier|\n|---|---|\n|The pursuer can’t directly see the pursued|-2|\n|The pursuer is flying but the pursued isn’t|+3|\n|The pursued is flying but the pursuer isn’t|-3|\n|A spotter is relaying the target’s position|+1|\n|Who knows the local terrain better?|-2 to +2|\n|The pursuit is half-hearted or obligatory|-1|\n|The pursuers are enraged or vengeful|+1|"
    },
