    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/tables/2-7-1-4-gaining-and-spending-skill-points",
      "@type": "Table",
      "name": "2.7.1.4 Gaining and Spending Skill Points",
      "slug": "2-7-1-4-gaining-and-spending-skill-points",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "2.7.1.4",
        "heading": "2.7.1.4 Gaining and Spending Skill Points",
        "lineStart": 3111,
        "lineEnd": 3129
      },
      "tableType": "2.7.1.4 Gaining and Spending Skill Points",
      "columns": [
        "Skill",
        "Point",
        "Min."
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "position": 1,
          "result": "Level",
          "cells": [
            "Level",
            "Cost",
            "Character Level"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 2,
          "result": "0",
          "cells": [
            "0",
            "1",
            "1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 3,
          "result": "1",
          "cells": [
            "1",
            "2",
            "1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 4,
          "result": "2",
          "cells": [
            "2",
            "3",
            "3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 5,
          "result": "3",
          "cells": [
            "3",
            "4",
            "6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 6,
          "result": "4",
          "cells": [
            "4",
            "5",
            "9"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "rulesText": "A PC who advances a level gains three skill points they can spend on improving their skills or save to spend later. Experts and Partial Experts with the Quick Learner class ability gain an extra bonus skill point to spend, giving them four points each time they advance.\n\nSkills that are gained or improved immediately on gaining a level are assumed to have been perfected over the past level and require no training time or teaching. If they save their skill points to spend them later then they’ll need to find some teacher or other explanation for developing them in the meanwhile.\n\nThe cost for improving a skill is listed below. Every skill level must be purchased in order; to gain level-1 in a skill you need to pay one point for level-0 and then two points for level-1. A PC must be the requisite minimum level to increase a skill to certain levels. Less hardened adventurers simply don’t have the focus and real-life experience to attain such a pitch of mastery.\n\nA PC cannot “partially buy” a skill level. If they don’t have enough skill points to buy a new level, they need to save them up until they can. A PC cannot develop skills beyond level-4.\n\n|Skill|Point|Min.|\n|---|---|---|\n|Level|Cost|Character Level|\n|0|1|1|\n|1|2|1|\n|2|3|3|\n|3|4|6|\n|4|5|9|"
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/tables/2-9-0-encumbrance",
      "@type": "Table",
      "name": "2.9.0 Encumbrance",
      "slug": "2-9-0-encumbrance",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "2.9.0",
        "heading": "2.9.0 Encumbrance",
        "lineStart": 3214,
        "lineEnd": 3231
      },
      "tableType": "2.9.0 Encumbrance",
      "columns": [
        "Gear",
        "Encumbrance"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "position": 1,
          "result": "Portable in a small pocket",
          "cells": [
            "Portable in a small pocket",
            "0 (Any reasonable number can be carried)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 2,
          "result": "Portable in one hand",
          "cells": [
            "Portable in one hand",
            "1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 3,
          "result": "Requires two hands to carry or use it",
          "cells": [
            "Requires two hands to carry or use it",
            "2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 4,
          "result": "Requires a whole-body effort to haul it",
          "cells": [
            "Requires a whole-body effort to haul it",
            "5+"
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 5,
          "result": "Dragging an unconscious teammate",
          "cells": [
            "Dragging an unconscious teammate",
            "12"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "rulesText": "Gear has encumbrance, measured in points, as example in the table below. The more awkward or bulky the object, the greater the encumbrance. The GM adjudicates ambiguous objects.\n\n|Gear|Encumbrance|\n|---|---|\n|Portable in a small pocket|0 (Any reasonable number can be carried)|\n|Portable in one hand|1|\n|Requires two hands to carry or use it|2|\n|Requires a whole-body effort to haul it|5+|\n|Dragging an unconscious teammate|12|\n\nGear is either Stowed or Readied. Stowed gear is packed away carefully in pockets, packs, and harnesses. It’s easier to carry but harder to quickly access. Using Stowed gear requires that the bearer take a Main Action to pull it out before using it. Readied gear is carried in hands, holsters, quick-access pockets, or other easily-accessible places. It can be used as part of an action without any further preparation.\n\nA character can carry a total number of Stowed encumbrance points equal to their Strength score. They can carry a number of Readied points equal to half their Strength, rounded down. Thus, a PC with a Strength score of 11 could carry 11 points of Stowed gear and 5 points of Readied.\n\nPCs can haul much heavier objects if necessary. If they push their limits for longer terms, they can carry an additional two Ready and four Stowed items. The first time they do this, their Move speed is cut by 30%, from 30 feet to 20 feet. The second time, it’s cut by 50%, from 20 feet to 10 feet. More weight than this can’t be practically hauled over significant distances."
    },
