      "rulesText": "speed, evasion, manual dexterity, reaction time, and combat initiative.",
      "category": "physical",
      "generationRule": "To generate their six attributes, the player rolls 3d6 in order, once for each attribute. At any point before section 1.5.0 in character creation the player may substitute a score of 14 for one rolled score.\n\nOptionally, a player may choose to assign their stats from the following array of numbers: 14, 12, 11, 10, 9, and 7, divided up as desired among the attributes. If an array is used a score may not be substituted with a 14 later.",
      "modifierTable": [
        {
          "sourceText": "Each attribute has a modifier, usually ranging from -2 to +2. This modifier is added to skill checks, attack rolls, damage rolls, Shock damage, and the relevant saving throw targets.\n\nAn attribute score of 3 has a modifier of -2. A score of 4-7 has a modifier of -1. A score of 8-13 has a modifier of +0. A score of 14-17 has a modifier of +1. A score of 18 has a modifier of +2.\n\nSome Foci and abilities may add bonuses or penalties to an attribute’s base modifier. Such bonuses or penalties cannot increase the modifier above +2 or below -2 unless explicitly indicated. Some injuries or character advancements may alter an attribute score; this new score may change the attribute’s modifier."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/attributes/intelligence",
      "@type": "Attribute",
      "name": "Intelligence",
      "slug": "intelligence",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.1.0",
        "heading": "1.1.0 Attributes",
        "lineStart": 269,
        "lineEnd": 290
      },
      "rulesText": "memory, reasoning, technical skills, and general education.",
      "category": "mental",
      "generationRule": "To generate their six attributes, the player rolls 3d6 in order, once for each attribute. At any point before section 1.5.0 in character creation the player may substitute a score of 14 for one rolled score.\n\nOptionally, a player may choose to assign their stats from the following array of numbers: 14, 12, 11, 10, 9, and 7, divided up as desired among the attributes. If an array is used a score may not be substituted with a 14 later.",
      "modifierTable": [
        {
          "sourceText": "Each attribute has a modifier, usually ranging from -2 to +2. This modifier is added to skill checks, attack rolls, damage rolls, Shock damage, and the relevant saving throw targets.\n\nAn attribute score of 3 has a modifier of -2. A score of 4-7 has a modifier of -1. A score of 8-13 has a modifier of +0. A score of 14-17 has a modifier of +1. A score of 18 has a modifier of +2.\n\nSome Foci and abilities may add bonuses or penalties to an attribute’s base modifier. Such bonuses or penalties cannot increase the modifier above +2 or below -2 unless explicitly indicated. Some injuries or character advancements may alter an attribute score; this new score may change the attribute’s modifier."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/attributes/strength",
      "@type": "Attribute",
      "name": "Strength",
      "slug": "strength",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.1.0",
        "heading": "1.1.0 Attributes",
        "lineStart": 269,
        "lineEnd": 290
      },
      "rulesText": "physical prowess, melee combat, carrying gear, and brute force.",
      "category": "physical",
      "generationRule": "To generate their six attributes, the player rolls 3d6 in order, once for each attribute. At any point before section 1.5.0 in character creation the player may substitute a score of 14 for one rolled score.\n\nOptionally, a player may choose to assign their stats from the following array of numbers: 14, 12, 11, 10, 9, and 7, divided up as desired among the attributes. If an array is used a score may not be substituted with a 14 later.",
      "modifierTable": [
        {
          "sourceText": "Each attribute has a modifier, usually ranging from -2 to +2. This modifier is added to skill checks, attack rolls, damage rolls, Shock damage, and the relevant saving throw targets.\n\nAn attribute score of 3 has a modifier of -2. A score of 4-7 has a modifier of -1. A score of 8-13 has a modifier of +0. A score of 14-17 has a modifier of +1. A score of 18 has a modifier of +2.\n\nSome Foci and abilities may add bonuses or penalties to an attribute’s base modifier. Such bonuses or penalties cannot increase the modifier above +2 or below -2 unless explicitly indicated. Some injuries or character advancements may alter an attribute score; this new score may change the attribute’s modifier."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/attributes/wisdom",
      "@type": "Attribute",
      "name": "Wisdom",
      "slug": "wisdom",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.1.0",
        "heading": "1.1.0 Attributes",
        "lineStart": 269,
        "lineEnd": 290
      },
      "rulesText": "noticing things, making judgments, reading situations, and intuition.",
      "category": "mental",
      "generationRule": "To generate their six attributes, the player rolls 3d6 in order, once for each attribute. At any point before section 1.5.0 in character creation the player may substitute a score of 14 for one rolled score.\n\nOptionally, a player may choose to assign their stats from the following array of numbers: 14, 12, 11, 10, 9, and 7, divided up as desired among the attributes. If an array is used a score may not be substituted with a 14 later.",
      "modifierTable": [
        {
          "sourceText": "Each attribute has a modifier, usually ranging from -2 to +2. This modifier is added to skill checks, attack rolls, damage rolls, Shock damage, and the relevant saving throw targets.\n\nAn attribute score of 3 has a modifier of -2. A score of 4-7 has a modifier of -1. A score of 8-13 has a modifier of +0. A score of 14-17 has a modifier of +1. A score of 18 has a modifier of +2.\n\nSome Foci and abilities may add bonuses or penalties to an attribute’s base modifier. Such bonuses or penalties cannot increase the modifier above +2 or below -2 unless explicitly indicated. Some injuries or character advancements may alter an attribute score; this new score may change the attribute’s modifier."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/administer",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Administer",
      "slug": "administer",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Administer: Keep an organization running smoothly, scribe things well, plan out logistics, identify incompetent or treacherous workers, analyze records or archives, or otherwise do things that an executive or middle-manager would need to do.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/connect",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Connect",
      "slug": "connect",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Connect: Find or know people who are useful to your purposes, make friendships or social acquaintances, know who to talk to get favors or services, and call on the help or resources of organizations you belong to. Connect covers your PC’s ability to find the people you need, though convincing them to help may require more than this.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/convince",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Convince",
      "slug": "convince",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Convince: Persuade a listener that something you are saying is true. Naturally, the more implausible the claim or more emotionally repugnant it is to them, the more difficult it is to persuade them. Furthermore, how they act on their newfound conviction is up to them and their motivations, and may not be perfectly predictable.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/craft",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Craft",
      "slug": "craft",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Craft: Craft or repair goods and technology appropriate to the PC’s background and society. The Craft skill can be used for a wide range of artisan pursuits, though a GM is within their rights to keep the PC from building complex things that are too far away from their past background and experience.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/exert",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Exert",
      "slug": "exert",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Exert: Run, swim, climb, jump, labor for long periods, throw things, or otherwise exert your physical strength, stamina, and coordination. Even a PC with poor physical attributes might have a good Exert skill reflecting athletic training and expertise in making the most of their available talents.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/heal",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Heal",
      "slug": "heal",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Heal: Treat wounds, cure diseases, neutralize poisons, diagnose psychological health issues, and otherwise tend to the wounds of body and mind. The Heal skill cannot cure lost hit points directly, but it’s a vital skill in stabilizing Mortally Wounded allies or ensuring clean recovery.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/know",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Know",
      "slug": "know",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Know: Know matters of history, geography, natural science, zoology, and other academic fields appropriate to a sage or scholar. While some sages might specialize in particular fields, most learned men and women in this age have a broad range of understanding, and will rarely be unable to even attempt to answer a question relevant to this skill.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/lead",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Lead",
      "slug": "lead",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Lead: Inspire others to follow your lead and believe in your plans and goals. Manage subordinates and keep them focused, loyal, and motivated in the face of danger or failure. A successful leader will keep their subordinate’s faith and confidence even when reason might make the leader’s plan appear questionable at best.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/magic",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Magic",
      "slug": "magic",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Magic: Cast or analyze magic and know things about famous mages or notable magical events. Classes that can’t cast spells obtain only intellectual and scholarly benefits from this skill.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/notice",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Notice",
      "slug": "notice",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Notice: Notice small details, impending ambushes, hidden features, or concealed objects. Detect subtle smells, sounds, or other sensory input. Notice cannot be used simply to detect a lie, but keen attention can often discern a subject’s emotional state.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/perform",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Perform",
      "slug": "perform",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Perform: Sing, act, dance, orate, or otherwise perform impressively for an audience. Compose music, plays, writings, or other works of performance art. Most performers will have a particular field they excel at, though polymaths might exist if the PC’s background is appropriate for such versatility.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/pray",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Pray",
      "slug": "pray",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Pray: Perform the clerical rites of your religion, and be familiar with the gods, demons, and taboos of major and minor faiths, and identify iconography and persons of religious importance. Pray also helps you know the state of local faiths and the important persons in their hierarchies.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/punch",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Punch",
      "slug": "punch",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Punch: Fight unarmed or with natural body weaponry. Punch, kick, grapple, or otherwise brawl without the benefit of man-made tools. This mode of fighting is inefficient at best without some special Focus to improve it, but it’s reliably non-lethal.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/ride",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Ride",
      "slug": "ride",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Ride: Ride an animal, drive a cart or carriage, or otherwise deal with land transportation. This skill also includes competence at mount care and tending, basic cart or carriage repair, judging good horseflesh, and other skills appropriate to a beast-rider of whatever society the PC comes from.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/sail",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Sail",
      "slug": "sail",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Sail: Sail or repair a ship, build small craft, navigate by the stars, read sea weather, manage sailors, and otherwise conduct the business of a professional mariner. This skill may apply to more esoteric means of vehicular travel in some societies.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/shoot",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Shoot",
      "slug": "shoot",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Shoot: Fire a bow or crossbow or throw a hurled weapon. Maintain ranged weaponry and fletch arrows.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/sneak",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Sneak",
      "slug": "sneak",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Sneak: Move silently, hide in shadows, avoid notice, pick pockets, disguise yourself, pick locks, defeat traps, or otherwise overcome security measures.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/stab",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Stab",
      "slug": "stab",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Stab: Fight with melee weapons or throw a hurled weapon. Maintain and identify weaponry.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/survive",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Survive",
      "slug": "survive",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Survive: Hunt, fish, navigate by the stars, mitigate environmental hazards, identify plants and wildlife, and craft basic survival tools and shelter. A PC’s Survive skill is most pertinent to the environments in their background, but the basic principles can be applied in all but the most alien environments.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/trade",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Trade",
      "slug": "trade",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "1.2.3",
        "heading": "1.2.3 The Skill List",
        "lineStart": 327,
        "lineEnd": 372
      },
      "rulesText": "Trade: Buy and sell at a profit, identify the worth of goods or treasures, deal with merchants and traders, find black-market goods and services, and know laws regarding smuggling and contraband.",
      "levels": [
        {
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "level": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/skills/work",
      "@type": "Skill",
      "name": "Work",
      "slug": "work",
      "source": {
