      },
      "traditionName": "high-magic",
      "level": 1,
      "effects": [
        {
          "sourceText": "A thaumic discharge is focused on a single visible creature within one hundred feet per caster level, wreathing them in a lethal mantle of crackling energy. The target suffers 1d8 damage per caster level, with a Physical save for half. NPC targets with only 1 hit die will inevitably be slain regardless of the damage done. The spell cannot be blocked by non-magical intervening barriers, provided the caster can see the target with their unaided vision."
        }
      ],
      "rulesText": "A thaumic discharge is focused on a single visible creature within one hundred feet per caster level, wreathing them in a lethal mantle of crackling energy. The target suffers 1d8 damage per caster level, with a Physical save for half. NPC targets with only 1 hit die will inevitably be slain regardless of the damage done. The spell cannot be blocked by non-magical intervening barriers, provided the caster can see the target with their unaided vision."
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/spells/the-dazzling-prismatic-hemicycle",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "The Dazzling Prismatic Hemicycle",
      "slug": "the-dazzling-prismatic-hemicycle",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "4.4.0",
        "heading": "The Dazzling Prismatic Hemicycle (Level 5)",
        "lineStart": 3922,
        "lineEnd": 3925
      },
      "tradition": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/classes/high-mage"
      },
      "traditionName": "high-magic",
      "level": 5,
      "effects": [
        {
          "sourceText": "A blinding fan of impossible colors cascades over all targets in front of the caster in an area equal to a cone a hundred feet long and a hundred feet wide at the end. Each creature within that area must make a Physical saving throw; those who fail roll 1d6. On a 1, they are unharmed, on a 2 they collapse into a handful of dust, on a 3 they fall unconscious for an hour, on a 4 they go violently insane for the next hour and attack all around them, on a 5 they turn to stone, and on a 6 they become utterly enthralled to the caster’s commands for the next hour, as if under the effect of an **_Ineluctable Shackles of Volition_** spell."
        }
      ],
      "rulesText": "A blinding fan of impossible colors cascades over all targets in front of the caster in an area equal to a cone a hundred feet long and a hundred feet wide at the end. Each creature within that area must make a Physical saving throw; those who fail roll 1d6. On a 1, they are unharmed, on a 2 they collapse into a handful of dust, on a 3 they fall unconscious for an hour, on a 4 they go violently insane for the next hour and attack all around them, on a 5 they turn to stone, and on a 6 they become utterly enthralled to the caster’s commands for the next hour, as if under the effect of an **_Ineluctable Shackles of Volition_** spell."
    },
    {
      "@context": "./context.jsonld",
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/spells/the-earth-as-clay",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "The Earth as Clay",
      "slug": "the-earth-as-clay",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/sources/wwn-srd-v1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "section": "4.4.0",
        "heading": "The Earth as Clay (Level 5)",
        "lineStart": 3942,
        "lineEnd": 3945
      },
      "tradition": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/wwn-system-json/objects/classes/high-mage"
      },
      "traditionName": "high-magic",
      "level": 5,
      "effects": [
        {
          "sourceText": "The caster molds the soil and stone of the land around them, raising hills, digging trenches, or forming simple structures out of extruded bedrock. Once cast, the mage may psychically mold the terrain within three hundred feet per caster level, shifting it slowly over the course of an hour to form whatever shape they desire out of it, provided the material used can actually maintain such a shape. Simple buildings and walls may be created out of bedrock or available stone, and tunnels and caves may be shaped up to 50 feet down from the caster, while hills may be raised up to 200 feet above the prevailing grade. This spell cannot work within a thousand feet of stone or earth that has been significantly worked by intelligent creatures, though the use of this spell by the same caster doesn’t count as working the earth on further castings."
        }
      ],
      "rulesText": "The caster molds the soil and stone of the land around them, raising hills, digging trenches, or forming simple structures out of extruded bedrock. Once cast, the mage may psychically mold the terrain within three hundred feet per caster level, shifting it slowly over the course of an hour to form whatever shape they desire out of it, provided the material used can actually maintain such a shape. Simple buildings and walls may be created out of bedrock or available stone, and tunnels and caves may be shaped up to 50 feet down from the caster, while hills may be raised up to 200 feet above the prevailing grade. This spell cannot work within a thousand feet of stone or earth that has been significantly worked by intelligent creatures, though the use of this spell by the same caster doesn’t count as working the earth on further castings."
    },
